{"assets":["/editorial-assets/0b43e8cde8c4ecafb00a8bf351742f16cacceeff7ef88b323039e2d89fc6624b.png"],"contestId":"276","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/276/problem/A"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Lunch Rush"}],"kind":"strong"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s look at all restraunts, where Rabbits can have their lunch. Let’s calculate the answer for all restraunts and choose the maximulm value among of them. We need to use formula descrbed in problem statement to calculate the answer for some particular restraunt. Time complexity of this solution is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/cJK5K017"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C++ code"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/D800mDax"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Java code"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/276/problem/B"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Little Girl and Game"}],"kind":"strong"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s calculate the number of letters with odd number of occurrences in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let this value be equal to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 0, then first player can win immediately: he can easily build palindrome, placing equal letters in different sides of resulting string (he always can do it, because total number of all letters is even). "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 1 then first player can win immediately again; at first he builds palindrome from letters with even number of occurrences in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"; after that he inserts the rest of the letters in the middle of built in previous step string. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s proof very useful statement. If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" > 1 our problem has the following solution: if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is even, than second player is winner; otherwise, first player is winner."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2. At the beginning of the game first player can make move of two types."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Using move of first type first player can decrease "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to 1 by erasing one appearance of letter with odd number of occurrences. But this move leads him to defeat, because after this move second player can build palindrome."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Using move of second type first player can increase "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to 3 by erasing one appearance of letter with even number of occurrences. In this case second player can make similar move — he will erase the same letter. Since the number of moves of this type is finite, sooner or later first player will have to make a move of first type. After this move he loses immediately."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So, if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2, than second player is a winner."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 3. First player can decrease "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to 2 by erasing the letter with odd number of occurrences. If second player will try to increase "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to 3 again by erasing the similar letter, first player can decrease "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to 2 again (he erases the same letter again). It’s easy to see that the last move in this sequence of moves will be the move of first player. So, first player always can change the game in such a way that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2. This position is losing position for second player and winning position for first player."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now we can easily proof our statement for any "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" using mathematical induction."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So, we have quite easy solution with time complexity "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"О"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"(|"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"S"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/FMDivpxx"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C++ code"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/AR641CLa"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Java code"}],"kind":"link"}],"