{"kind":"text","text":"First of all we should convert "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the binary numeral system. Now we can solve our problem with dynamic programming, using the following state "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2]["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2], where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is current position in binary representation of our numbers "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (this parameter is in range from 0 to number of bits in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"), "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (0 or 1) is a variable, which shows if current value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"а"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is strictly greater than "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 (от 0 до 1) is a variable, which shows if current value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"а"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is strictly less then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 are variables, which show the similar things for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s use recursion with memorization for our solution."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s define the base of recursion. If we have looked through all the bits, we should return 0."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s define a recursive transition. We need to know, which bits we can place into binary representation of number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"а"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th position. We can place 0 if the following condition is true: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bit of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to 0, or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bit of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to 1 and variable "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 shows that current value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is strictly greater then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Similarly, we can place 1 if the following condition is true: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bit of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to 1, or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bit of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is equal to 0 and variable "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 shows that current value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is strictly less then "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Similarly, we can obtain, which bits we can place into binary representation of number "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th position. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s iterate through all possible bits’ values and check the result of xor operation. If it is equal to 1, we should add to the answer corresponding power of 2. We also need carefully recalculate values of variables "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"1, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fl"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"fr"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"2. We should choose maximum answer from all valid options."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Initial state for our recursion is ("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"P"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":",0,0,0,0), where "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"P"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is number of bits in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I hope, my code will clarify all the obscure points."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"I also want to say, that this approach is in some sense universal and can be applied to many similar problems, "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/261/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"like this one"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The complexity of algorithm is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"logR"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/T58pdAzc"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C++ code"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/t3cTWuCn"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Java code"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In Russian thread I saw another really nice solution, so I decided to include this solution to the editorial."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First of all, if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", than the answer is 0."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now let’s consider case with "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≠ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bit of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" be the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bit of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Let’s define "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" as largest number such as "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≠ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"subscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" (we use 0-based indexation). Let’s take a look at all numbers in range ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":";"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]. It’s easy to see, that bits, that are higher than bit with index "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" are equal for all this numbers. Thus, those bits can not affect our answer, because their xor will always equal to 0. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s build numbers "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the following way:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1) "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":": bits which are higher than bit with index "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" are equal to the corresponding bits of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bit is equal to 0, the rest of bits are equal to 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1) "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":": bits which are higher than bit with index "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" are equal to the corresponding bits of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th bit is equal to 1, the rest of bits are equal to 0."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It’s easy to see, that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" both lie in range ["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"L"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":";"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"R"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"]. It’s also easy to see, that xor of this numbers sets all bits, that are not higher than bit with index "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to 1. So, our answer is maximum possible and is equal to 2"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1"}],"kind":"superscript"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1 "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The complexity of algorithm is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"logR"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/276/submission/3184866"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Java solution"}],"kind":"link"},{"kind":"text","text":" from "},{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/profile/AlexanderBolshakov"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"AlexanderBolshakov"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We can iterate through value of "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" using binary search. We can achieve time complexity "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"log"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"logR"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")) in this way, but it wasn’t required during the contest."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/276/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Little Girl and Problem on Trees"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"strong"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"One can see, that our tree is a set of chains, each of which starts in the root. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"First of all we need to decompose our tree in chains using, for example, depth first search. For each vertex we should find out it’s depth and number of chain, which contain this vertex. For each chain we’ll use some data structure, which can fast enough change it’s elements and fast enough answer to the range sum query. For example, we canuse Binary Indexed Tree (BIT). We also need to create one BIT for root. This BIT is global: it’s information is actual for all the chains"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s remember problem "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"С"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". In that problem we used array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"d"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" for processing all the queries. We need to know values of elements of array "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"b"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" in that problem after processing all the queries. In this problem queries are online. That’s why we need to use BIT; it allows to change element and answer range sum query in "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"logN"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") time."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s learn, how to process queries, which require modification and queries, which require finding the element, using BIT."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"BIT can make two types of operations:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"add"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") — add value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"y"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to element with index "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"find"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") – finds sum in range from 1 to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"x"}],"kind":"emphasis"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s consider, that we need to add value "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"val"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to all elements in range from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" . Than we should just make operations "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"add"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"l"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"val"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":") and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"add"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"r"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1,  - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"val"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let’s consider, that we have query which require printing the value of element with index "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Then we should just make operation "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"find"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"v"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now let’s go back to the initial problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"During the processing query of type 0 we should check, if it affects the root. If query affects the root, we should carefully process this query in our chain and make necessary changes in root’s BIT. Otherwise we just process query in our chain."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"During the processing query of type 1 we should just find corresponding sums in root’s BIT and in BIT for our chain. We should print the sum of this values. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Time complexity of this solution is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"O"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"N"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"QlogN"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/w8ybNR2z"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C++ code"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"http://pastebin.com/NDt1DXyx"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Java code"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"That’s all. I’ll be very glad to answer to your question in comments."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/6779"}